WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.736
[music playing]

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.098 line:0%
CALE HUGHES:
Operationally, it works

00:00:33.198 --> 00:00:35.301 line:7%
just like a laser pointer.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.871 line:0%
There's a chamber inside
with special materials

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:38.671 line:7%
that release photons.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.012 line:0%
INEZ KELLY: If you're
looking at a boat coming in

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.149 line:0%
over the water, you can
target exactly the engine

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:52.051 line:0%
and take out exactly the
engine, and not necessarily

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:54.153 line:7%
damage anything else.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:57.089 line:0%
And that type of
precision weapon work

00:00:57.189 --> 00:00:58.925 line:0%
is something that
you don't really

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.527 line:0%
get with conventional
weapons, because there tends

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:04.130 line:7%
to be more collateral damage.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.531 line:0%
CHRIS WELLS: It's
useful against a variety

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:07.333 line:7%
of threats, surface or air.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:10.703 line:0%
It's not a niche weapon
system like some other weapons

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.204 line:0%
that we have throughout
the military,

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:14.173 line:0%
where it's only good
against air contacts,

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:17.543 line:0%
or it's only good
against surface targets.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.613 line:7%
[music playing]

